# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the region-read qualification pack (tp4-kvread-next-jobs, docs/prefix-audit-cost.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the cost.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env).
# Q2 (THE CROSS CHECK on a real prompt): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-audit-r2-kvx is A0's audited control (the Lever N audit, no parked engines) plus QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_KV_READ=cross. The first digest reads the
# KV through the extension AND every cache whole, compares the two selections byte for byte and digests the WHOLE-cache bytes (one whole-pool read, about 8.4 minutes, inside a boot the job pays anyway); every later digest
# is the region read alone. warmup then levern_equal: the exact-length prompts (4,097 to 32,785 tokens) each log a digest line, and each is followed by a '[PINDIAG] lever N kv read mode=cross' line.
# READ, in order, stopping at the first failure: (1) one '[PINDIAG] lever N kv read ready mode=cross' line at the attach; (2) exactly one '[PINDIAG] lever N kv read cross req= tensors=<n> mismatched=0 ... fallback=-' line
# with tensors > 0 (a mismatch is the extension's finding: NOT QUALIFIED, and the first suspects are the host tensor's shape, several region reads of one shard in one enqueue and the program cache); (3) a 'kv read mode=cross'
# line per digest with fallback=- (a fallback means the region read did not answer); (4) c2_smoke_check clean (its levern_kv_read_problems rule); (5) levern_compare.py of this job's container log against any full-read arm's
# (A0 of the engine-reuse pack) for the prompts in common: every digest equal. Duration (estimate): 45 minutes. Stop rule: a mismatch or an absent cross line stops the pack's audited jobs (A0R and A1R are skipped).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-audit-r2-kvx
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,levern_equal
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=cross-check arm (exactness test): its test list is fixed by the pack protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
